# Some files here are verified by their BYTES, not by parsing them: an evidence manifest is
# hashed, a mass mesh is compared exactly, a GLB is a digest in a receipt. Git's autocrlf - the
# default on Windows - rewrites line endings on checkout, which added one byte to
# evidence-manifest.json and made a fresh clone refuse `prepare creative-020` while the same
# file worked in the repository it had been committed from. Nothing under these paths may be
# EOL-converted.
data/datasets/** -text
data/sources/** -text
output/** -text
test/fixtures/** -text
*.glb -text
*.obj -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
